rtsHelp:"Newick and NEXUS export the working tree, but cannot retain all imported XML annotations. Use a Tree document to retain everything, or Original input for the unchanged source. Tables export nodes, edges or edit history.",tableViewHelp:"Tips lists terminal nodes and their sample metadata. All nodes also includes internal nodes, which may have no sample values. Edges lists branch lengths and support; History lists edits.",metricHelp:"Automatic uses imported distances when they remain readable, but uses topology-only spacing for circular trees that would be severely compressed. Branch lengths always forces true distance scaling when lengths are available. Topology only aligns displayed terminals in rooted rectangular and circular views; unrooted view uses equal topological segments. These display choices never change the original values.",spacingHelp:"Sets the minimum distance between tip rows. Circular layouts also grow to make room for labels.",ladderizeHelp:"Sorts sibling clades by their number of tips. This changes their order in the figure, not their relationships or branch lengths.",branchShapeHelp:"Changes how connecting branches are drawn. Imported topology and branch lengths stay unchanged.",unrootedAlgorithmHelp:"Equal angle allocates angles by tip counts. Equal daylight rotates clades to balance the empty angles between them while preserving edge lengths. Some trees may still overlap.",labelAlignmentHelp:"Aligned places labels at a common outer edge. At tips places them beside their terminal nodes. Metadata tracks follow the label positions.",showBranchLengthsHelp:"Displays each edge\\u2019s imported length, including internal edges. These are not root-to-tip distances. Units depend on the source tree.",branchLengthPrecisionHelp:"Rounds displayed lengths only. Very small nonzero values use scientific notation instead of appearing as zero; exact values remain in tooltips and downloads.",supportFieldHelp:"Choose the imported support measure to display. Numbers can show all fields; symbols and colors use one field, identified in the legend. The viewer does not calculate support values.",supportMinimumHelp:"Used when Display density is Minimum value. Values remain in the selected field\\u2019s original units: for example, 90 for a percent field or 0.9 for a proportion field.",supportFilterHelp:"Automatic uses a 95% (or 0.95 proportion) minimum in dense circular views with declared support units. All values removes filtering; Below maximum shows values below 100% or 1.0, and Minimum value uses your cutoff. Labels move locally to avoid collisions; any that cannot fit are counted explicitly. Every value remains in Selection, the Edges table and data downloads.",supportPrecisionHelp:"Rounds displayed support values without changing the imported evidence.",supportSizeHelp:"Sets the support text size or the maximum symbol diameter. Symbol size varies over the selected field\\u2019s observed range.",supportPositionHelp:"Prefers the child node or its incoming branch. Numbers automatically move around the local tree geometry to clear nearby branches and labels; a fine connector identifies the node or branch when extra space is needed. Symbols stay at the chosen position.",supportProfileHelp:"Numeric internal labels may be node names or support values. Choose the meaning from the producing program\\u2019s report. Interpretation is undoable and does not rescale values.",circularRotationHelp:"Rotates the circular tree clockwise in degrees, without changing its root or relationships.",circularArcHelp:"Sets how much of the circle is occupied by the tree. A smaller arc leaves an opening for annotations and labels.",showScaleHelp:"Shows a ruler in the source tree\\u2019s branch-length units. It is available when the figure uses branch lengths, rather than topology-only spacing.",trackFieldHelp:"Fields come from the current metadata table. Import your own table to replace these columns; rows must match exact tip labels or node IDs.",trackTypeHelp:"Color strips and symbols show categories; bars and heatmaps require numeric fields. Text shows field values directly. Grouped bars compare several numeric fields on a shared scale.",extraBarFieldsHelp:"Choose additional numeric fields with comparable units. All bars in this track share one scale; missing values remain distinct from zero.",cladeBracketHelp:"Adds a named bracket outside the labels and tracks. If the group becomes separated by reordering or rerooting, each contiguous part gets a bracket.",styleScopeHelp:"Selected node changes one node\\u2019s appearance. Selected clade applies the appearance to that node and its descendants. Scientific values stay unchanged.",rootHereHelp:"Moves the root to the selected internal node while preserving tip-to-tip distances and branch evidence. This edits the tree and can be reversed with Undo.",rootOnBranchHelp:"Places the root halfway along the branch leading to the selected tip or clade. Select an outgroup tip or outgroup clade to use this common rooting method. Tip-to-tip distances and branch evidence are preserved, and Undo restores the prior root.",editDisplayName:"Edit display name",saveChanges:"Save",editMetadata:"Edit metadata",noRows:"No matching rows",page:"Page",currentNode:"Current node",settings:"Settings",closeSettings:"Hide settings",tracksTab:"Tracks",treeLayout:"Tree layout",documentSettings:"Document",exportMenu:"Export",figureHeading:"Figure",symbol:"Symbols","multi-bar":"Grouped bars",barScaleHelp:"Choose fields with comparable units; grouped bars share one numeric scale.",supportThresholdHelp:"Values use the selected field\\u2019s original units; leave blank to show all values.",extraBarFields:"Additional numeric fields (select one or more)",symbolShape:"Symbol shape",circleSymbol:"Circle",squareSymbol:"Square",triangleSymbol:"Triangle",printPdf:"Print / PDF",printTitle:"Tree Viewer figure",cladeAnnotation:"Clade annotation",cladeLabel:"Clade name",cladeColor:"Shading color",cladeOp